Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:17:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m21
 (14z-185)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged29/rompath/vsavjw.zip by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py in the
consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

EIGHT members moved, and they are the M21 delta exactly (the consuming tree's
build/agent185/m21/deltas_measurer.txt):
  vm3j.03d  0dbc14a6 -> e537ef29   program: the two new sites — #159's facing
                                   resolver (0x01886C) and #182's block entry
                                   (0x02393A)
  vm3j.04d  3e4098b8 -> d522cfe7   program: placement shifted by the two
  vm3j.07b  b845aef9 -> 8f131ac1   thunks (Donovan's at 0x3FFD60, Phobos's at
  vm3j.10b  05cdacd0 -> b1a24511   0x4718D0); every relocation target
  vsw.41    c47529fa -> 02991388   content-identical
  vsw.42    7823ef8e -> 5b75ebbd
  vsw.33m   70bc7941 -> 27a0fd82   group-C glyphs, the M20 -> M21 mark
  vsw.37m   aba94e63 -> b759cc68   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NZtrb3GCyt4TpaeTSbQL4N
